# TiltUpPanel

Active project. FlattenMod is shipped and off-limits. SplineGradeMod is a
separate plugin — do not edit it unless asked. InsetMod is on hold (prior
art for Phase 2 reveal carve).

Read `TiltUpPanel/TiltUpPanel_Handoff.md` before changing create-mouse,
paramblock, or `BuildMesh`. Spec: `TiltUpPanel/TiltUpPanel_ProjectSpec.md`.

Hard rules:
- Object plugin: `SimpleObject2`, output `.dlo` (not `.dlm`).
- Do not run MSBuild or copy the `.dlo`. User builds Hybrid | x64 from Visual Studio.
- `BuildMesh()` regenerates from the pblock every time. No cached mesh. No boolean solver.
- ParamBlockDesc2 4th arg is `&tiltUpPanelDesc`, terminator is `p_end`. Tab params need `P_VARIABLE_SIZE`.
- Local space: X = width, Y = thickness, Z = height. Origin = lower-left-back. Base front at y = depth; panel caps at y = depth + grooveDepth.
- Python editor (Phase 3) writes pblock only — never touches geometry.
- Verify unknown SDK signatures with Go to Definition in this Max 2027 SDK, not memory.
- Groove width/depth are global scalars. Reveals are axis + position Tabs only.
- Build the base box with the full front grid first. Panel extrusions are additional geometry; do not move or delete those front quads. Do not reintroduce a boolean solver.
